slurm-spank-plugin-ebpf-exporter (0.1-0sci9u1) scibian9; urgency=medium

  * debian/rules: build and install through the upstream Makefile, with
    SLURM_LIBDIR set to /usr/lib/slurm and the plugstack snippet installed as
    /etc/slurm/plugstack.conf.d/ebpf.conf. The RPM path (/usr/lib64/slurm)
    written in the sample snippet is rewritten at install time.
  * debian/rules: append -fPIC and -shared to the flags exported by
    dpkg-buildflags, which would otherwise override the upstream defaults and
    break the link of the shared object.
  * debian/control: describe the plugin, depend on systemd (the plugin drives
    ebpf_exporter with systemctl), bump to debhelper compat 10.
  * Drop debian/slurm-spank-plugin-ebpf-exporter.install, superseded by the Makefile
    install target.
  * Add README.Debian documenting the install paths, the two modes and the
    submission-host requirement of opt-in mode.

